00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
Many Christmas stories have been adapted to feature films and TV specials,
and have been broadcast and repeated many times on television.

15
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Since the popularization of home video in the 1980s, these films are sold
and re-sold every year during the holiday shopping season.

16
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Many television networks, film studios, and production companies, such as cable television channels Hallmark and Lifetime, produce and
release new Christmas-themed films every year during or around December, all with variations of similar plots and themes.

17
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
Additionally, films revolving around the Nativity story of Christmas are regularly
produced such as The Nativity Story (2006) and The Star (2017).

18
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
One film that has become the flashpoint for "Is this a Christmas movie or not?" debates is Die Hard (1988), with some viewing the film as a
Christmas movie intertwined with an action genre setting or a film that is simply set around the Christmas and holiday season.

19
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:54,000
The tone is emotional.
